    <title>Giuga Numbers and the arithmetic derivative</title>
    <updated>2011-03-11T15:50:38Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1103.2298v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1103.2298v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We characterize Giuga Numbers as solutions to the equation $n'=an+1$, with $a \in \mathbb{N}$ and $n'$ being the arithmetic derivative. Although this fact does not refute Lava's conjecture, it brings doubts about its veracity.</summary>
